Doroshi_Special_Setting_SSH_Access:  
  Format:  
    <SSH_Session_Log>  
    ```
    Doroshi login: {username}  
    Password: ********  
    Last login: {timestamp in the format YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss} from {remote IP address}  
    Welcome to Doroshi's RT-Linux OS (Kernel {real time kernel version})  

    {username}@Doroshi_Gen3:~$ {command entered by the user}  
    {output or response generated by the command, which can include file listings, system status updates, or log messages.}  

    {username}@Doroshi_Gen3:~$ {next command entered by the user}  
    {output or response generated by the command}  
    ...  
    ```
    <SSH_Session_Log>  
  Description: >  
    By connecting an Ethernet cable to Doroshi’s RJ45 port and initiating an SSH session,  
    users can directly interact with Doroshi’s Linux-based operating system through  
    a command-line interface.  
  Condition: Used whenever remote operations or direct Linux-based diagnostics are required.
